   "description": "Surrender is the giving up of self-governance — the inner act of letting go of one's claim to control one's own life, resources, or outcome. The Hebrew vocabulary here is built around the root for closing, shutting, and the coming out that happens when a city falls to a siege: surrender is what happens when resistance ends. In Scripture, surrender to God is not defeat but the beginning of genuine life: the self that is surrendered to God is not destroyed but restored. The theology of surrender runs through the entire biblical account of what it means to trust.",
